sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant G as Credit grant API
    participant W as Usage worker
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over G,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C<br/>Event row: usage_inbox.source = S and usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Request advisory identity: api_idempotency_operations.operation_scope<br/>plus api_idempotency_operations.idempotency_key (not a row lock)<br/>Catalog advisory (65102, 2): protects price_versions, not a column
    Note over G,D: Initial credit 0, usage gross 3 cents, grant 2 cents.<br/>Each branch starts from that same isolated state.
    alt Grant gets the account first
        G->>D: BEGIN, scoped request lock<br/>FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        W->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        Note over W,D: WAIT for the credit grant
        G->>D: INSERT credit_entries, add 2 cents to account<br/>Store request result, COMMIT
        D-->>W: Account lock granted, credit is 2 cents
        W->>D: Shared catalog lock, FOR UPDATE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Allocate 2 cents, persist group and debit, COMMIT
        Note over W,D: Usage net 1 cent, remaining credit 0
    else Worker gets the account first
        W->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        G->>D: BEGIN, scoped request lock<br/>FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        Note over G,D: WAIT for the worker
        W->>D: Rate gross 3 cents with no allocated credit, COMMIT
        D-->>G: Account lock granted
        G->>D: Grant 2 cents and store request result, COMMIT
        Note over G,D: Usage net remains 3 cents, remaining credit 2 cents.<br/>A later grant does not rewrite the earlier allocation.
    end
    Note over G,D: Two new grant keys add under this same account lock.<br/>An identical grant key replays through the request lock.
